{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Moment of Inversion.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Moment of Inversion.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"moment of inversion moment of inversion","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Moment of Inversion.md","fileName":"Moment of Inversion.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Moment of Inversion","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 15:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Level and Scene Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Level and Scene Design","Game Pacing","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Moment of Inversion.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Moment of Inversion.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"moment of inversion moment of inversion","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Moment of Inversion.md","fileName":"Moment of Inversion.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Moment of Inversion","heading":"Moment of Inversion","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A moment of inversion is a sudden change in a game's dominant relationship, such as the hunted becoming the hunter or a background rule moving to the foreground. It changes the shape of play and often functions as a climax or release.\n\nInversion creates contrast within [[Game Pacing|pacing]] by briefly changing roles, priorities, or power. Because it reuses established rules in a different relationship, it can feel surprising while remaining understandable.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Level and Scene Design","Game Pacing","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Moment of Inversion.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Moment of Inversion.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"moment of inversion moment of inversion","filePath":"6 - Full No